[agent] The deliverable is complete. Summary of what was done — entirely on the platform via the `hops` CLI:
[agent] 1. **Ingested** `data/feature_history.csv` (567 rows) into feature group `feature_history` v1 with composite primary key `account_id,event_time` so every revision is preserved (a single-key FG would have upserted away the history).
[agent] 2. **Point-in-time selection + scoring ran on the platform** via Trino SQL over the offline store (Delta-backed `delta.mlpab6690f4_featurestore.feature_history_1`):
[agent]    - `row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY account_id ORDER BY event_time DESC)` filtered to `event_time <= 1773594000000` (T) → picks the most recent revision **at or before T**, ignoring later revisions.
[agent]    - `score = round(1/(1+exp(-(-0.7952·f1 + 0.3018·f2 - 0.8863·f3 - 0.2124))), 6)` — the model's logistic sigmoid, rounded to 6 decimals.
[agent]    - All 80 distinct accounts have a revision ≤ T, so all 80 were scored.
[agent] 3. **Produced `scores656c6b` v1** — online-enabled feature group, record key `account_id`, exactly columns `account_id, score`, 80 rows (one per account). `Online: yes` so the features are available for low-latency real-time lookup as well as offline; the insert materialized both stores.
[agent] Verified: `hops fg info` shows `Online: yes`, PK `account_id`; `hops fg preview` shows the `account_id, score` schema with rounded scores (e.g. A0001→0.904106, A0004→0.522101). The float display artifacts like `0.45925499999999997` are just double-repr of the stored 6-decimal value `0.459255`.
